# Error handling

## Pipeline
- Interceptor order: `applicationHeader → language → csrf → **error**`
- `ApiErrorHandler` applies auth side-effects and publishes user-facing errors to `GlobalErrorService`
- `GlobalErrorService.show()` calls `ApplicationRef.tick()` — required in zoneless when HTTP/RxJS emits outside Angular
- **Display only in layouts** (never per-page):
  - `AuthLayout` → `<app-global-error-banner variant="auth" />` (login, register, etc.)
  - `ShellLayout` → `<app-global-error-banner variant="shell" />` (workspace pages)

## Components MUST NOT
- Add local `error` signals or `@if (error())` panels for HTTP failures
- Catch HTTP errors solely to display `failure.message` — the interceptor already did that
- Parse `HttpErrorResponse` or ProblemDetails in feature code

## Allowed
- `HttpContextToken` `SILENT_ERROR` on requests that must not show the global banner (rare)
- Catch errors only for non-display control flow (e.g. stopping a spinner) — never duplicate messaging
- Client-side form validation stays in Signal Forms schemas; server `Validation` field errors appear globally

## ProblemDetails contract
| Status | Code examples | Notes |
|--------|---------------|-------|
| 400 | `Validation`, `Request.InvalidBody`, `Auth.AntiforgeryFailed` | `errors` map for field messages |
| 401 | `Auth.NotAuthenticated`, `Auth.InvalidCredentials` | Authenticated API 401 → local logout → `/login`; public auth failures (login etc.) stay + banner; `Auth.SessionExpired` → `/session-expired` |
| 403 | `Auth.PermissionDenied` | includes `requiredPermissions` |
| 404 | `*.NotFound` | domain-specific |
| 409 | `*.EmailAlreadyExists`, business conflict | domain-specific |
| 422 | business validation | domain-specific |
| 429 | `Request.RateLimitExceeded` | `Retry-After` header when present |
| 500 | `System.UnexpectedError` | generic fallback message |

## Auth side-effects (ApiErrorHandler only)
- `Auth.AntiforgeryFailed` → invalidate CSRF token
- `Auth.ApplicationAccessDenied` + navigable `redirectUrl` → SSO redirect
- `Identity.LoginIntent.*` → clear intent + scrub URL
- `Auth.SessionExpired` → mark anonymous → `/session-expired`
- Authenticated API 401 (coded or not) → mark anonymous → `/login`
- Public auth 401s (`/auth/login`, register, password flows) and `Auth.InvalidCredentials` → stay + banner
- Bootstrap probes (`/auth/me`, `/auth/companies`, `/auth/csrf`) → silent (no banner)

## i18n
- Display `message.en` / `message.ar` from ProblemDetails via `normalizeError`
- Global banner strings use `errors.*` keys
